<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Simple Utilities: Wall (Owlchemist.WallUtilities) - alive, declares 1.5 and 1.6.

  Owl_Fencepost_TorchLamp is in 1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Buildings/Fencepost_Lights.xml, unchanged,
  and still has its own <comps>.

  MysticFelines' file carried the comment "Ideology" over this operation, copied from the file
  next to it. The fencepost torch has nothing to do with Ideology; the comment is dropped rather
  than corrected in place, since it was never describing this patch.

  Every conditional also carries [not(comps/li[@Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker"])].
  Patches apply in mod load order and this mod loads after Simple FX: Smoke, so its comps are
  already in the document when these run. If it ever adds one of these buildings to its own
  patches, the operation here stands down instead of adding a second comp and doubling the
  smoke - a collision a defName test cannot see, because the def exists either way.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Owl_Fencepost_TorchLamp"][not(comps/li[@Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker"])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Owl_Fencepost_TorchLamp"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker">
          <fleckDef>Owl_Vapor</fleckDef>
          <particleSize>0.4</particleSize>
          <particleOffset>(0,0,0.6)</particleOffset>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
